{"timestamp": "2026-06-17T06:36:44.282128+00:00", "trace_id": "a1074832-da68-449a-9b69-df818737adec", "strategy": "program_of_thought", "problem_id": "gsm8k-test-57", "step_type": "reasoning_step", "inputs": {"kind": "run_start", "question": "A wooden bridge can carry no more than 5000 pounds. A delivery truck filled with identical boxes, each weighing 15 pounds, will pass over the bridge. The combined weight of the driver and the empty truck is 3755 pounds. What is the maximum number of boxes which can be loaded onto the truck while not exceeding the bridge's weight limit?"}, "outputs": {}, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency_ms": null, "metadata": {}}
{"timestamp": "2026-06-17T06:37:03.721747+00:00", "trace_id": "a1074832-da68-449a-9b69-df818737adec", "strategy": "program_of_thought", "problem_id": "gsm8k-test-57", "step_type": "reasoning_step", "inputs": {"kind": "thought", "data": {"attempt": 1}}, "outputs": {"content": "Let `n` be the number of boxes.  \nTotal weight = driver+truck + 15*n = 3755 + 15*n.  \nRequire 3755 + 15*n ≤ 5000 → 15*n ≤ 1245 → n ≤ 83.  \nMaximum whole boxes is 83."}, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency_ms": null, "metadata": {}}
{"timestamp": "2026-06-17T06:37:03.721747+00:00", "trace_id": "a1074832-da68-449a-9b69-df818737adec", "strategy": "program_of_thought", "problem_id": "gsm8k-test-57", "step_type": "reasoning_step", "inputs": {"kind": "code", "data": {"attempt": 1}}, "outputs": {"content": "driver_truck = 3755\nbox_weight = 15\nmax_weight = 5000\nmax_boxes = (max_weight - driver_truck) // box_weight\nprint(max_boxes)"}, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency_ms": null, "metadata": {}}
